{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And it sat in strength.</b> In place of 'his bow.'" "ויפוזו, and they grew strong, and close to it is מפזז (2 Samuel 6:16). And some interpret it from פז [fine gold], but it has no meaning." "And the meaning: the owners of arrows hated him, and banded together to pour out his bitterness, but his bow was strong and they were in fear of him; they could not overcome him, for his hands were strong." "<b>From the hand of the Mighty One of Jacob, from there.</b> A hint: 'the Mighty One of Jacob' — He is HaShem; from that power he was able, and he was the Shepherd of the Stone of Israel, and so it was, and he sustained Joseph. And the meaning of 'the Mighty One of Jacob' is that he knew his love for Joseph." "And the meaning of 'stone' is like the substance of the matter. And some say that משם is like מאז [from of old], and its like we have not found in all of Scripture. Also 'the Stone of Israel': he set his heart and was like a stone, and returned to shepherd, and the meaning is to keep alive by means of food. And this is a far-fetched way."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:35.866427400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}